ok   PathSyntax.decode is private
ok   Set-Cookie: both values are sent
ok   []= replaces values case-insensitively
ok   managed and invalid headers are rejected
ok   PathSyntax.segments does not modify input
ok   PathSyntax.segments decodes UTF-8
ok   parameter names are computed at registration
ok   PathSyntax.params
-- HttpNative compared with reference HttpSyntax
ok   browser request uses C fast path
ok   constructed cases match reference (41)
ok   mutation fuzzing: 4000 cases; no mismatches
ok   some mutations use fast path (true)
-- Pool: kill during checkout
ok   resources remain after 300 killed threads
-- Router: seal and parameters
ok   routes cannot be added after seal!
ok   DELETE route and shared empty params
-- Pool: boundary cases
ok   negative max_lifetime is rejected
ok   second thread waits for resource
ok   kill while waiting for resource does not lose capacity
-- HttpNative: scan_at boundaries
ok   scan_at within data bounds
ok   scan_at outside data bounds -> reject
ok   scan_at with negative start -> reject
-- Response: body without copy
ok   payload returns original body object
ok   non-ASCII body is serialized byte-for-byte
-- C byte checks compared with regexes
ok   Host: C matches regex on 3029 inputs
ok   token: C matches regex
ok   ctl: C matches regex
ok   digits: C matches regex
-- Pool: kill at different stages
ok   after kill during factory/validate/block/close: invariant and quarantine
-- HTTP: limits
ok   Content-Length longer than 9 digits with large max_body
ok   Content-Length exceeds max_body -> too_long
ok   invalid server options are rejected (9)
-- Pool: deterministic interruptions (test holds pool mutex)
ok   resource return does not wait for pool mutex
ok   kill while waiting for checkout mutex leaves accounting unchanged
ok   infinite max_lifetime is rejected
ok   after stage stress: open == idle + out; no resource remains checked out
-- Pool: physical capacity during close
ok   slot remains occupied while resource is closing
ok   second request waits instead of opening an extra resource
ok   second request gets new resource after close
ok   live resources never exceed size
ok   close failure is counted and slot remains quarantined
ok   stale-close counts fatal error and keeps slot
ok   close start without result keeps slot occupied
ok   late and duplicate close result is applied once
